Based on the search results, the "Vauxhall Omega i V6" most likely refers to a model from the Omega A generation (1986-1993), specifically the 3.0i V6 24V variant. The 1993 model year is a good representation of the later "i" models. Specs vary slightly between sources, but I will use the most consistent figures found for the 3.0i 24V engine.

- Engine: 3.0L V6 (24v)
- HP: ~201-207 hp
- Torque: ~195-199 lb-ft
- 0-60 mph: ~7.6-8.3 seconds (Using 8.0s as a middle ground)
- Top Speed: ~149 mph
- Drive Type: RWD
- Transmission: Available with Manual or Automatic. I will score for Automatic as per previous requests.
- Dimensions: Length ~4.7m, Wheelbase ~2.73m
- Body Style: Sedan or Estate. Scoring for Sedan.
- Seats: 5
- Cargo Space: ~18.4 cu ft (Sedan)
- Ground Clearance: ~5.9 inches (for a later model, likely similar)
- MPG: ~22-27 MPG (Combined NEDC). Real-world likely lower. Using 24 MPG as a mid-point.
- CO2: ~251-255 g/km
- Reliability: Mixed reviews, some sources mention problems, others decent for later models. Generally considered below average compared to modern cars. -0.50 seems appropriate.
- Insurance Group: Omega models from 1994-2003 range, some V6 models are in Group 29. Group 29 is above average. -0.20 seems fair.

